AUDIO: 'macOS is remarkably good at looking after itself. Anyone who\'s watched a Windows install slow to a crawl over the years knows exactly how well-tuned it is by comparison.'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But the operating system and the apps we install on our Macs do have one irritating flaw. They\'re not brilliant at tidying up after themselves. And long-forgotten directories, the remnants of long-since'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uninstalled apps, cache and log files often end up taking a stupid amount of space up on our SSDs. The good news is you don\'t need to pay a'

